IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa7-ch3a.l4: Part 13 Chapter 3, Resolutions at meetings: general provisions and calling meetings (ss 301 to 306),
-- lines 3887-3941 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4.

§ `Part 13 Chapter 3 -- Resolutions at meetings`

§§ `General provisions about resolutions at meetings`

-- ---- s 301 Resolutions at general meetings -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3890 | A resolution of the members of a company is validly passed at a general meeting if—
-- src:3891 | (a) notice of the meeting and of the resolution is given, and
-- src:3892 | (b) the meeting is held and conducted,
-- src:3893 | in accordance with the provisions of this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles.
@ref s 301 Resolutions at general meetings (src:3890-3893)
GIVEN `notice of the meeting and of the resolution is given in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held and conducted in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 301 the resolution is validly passed at the general meeting` MEANS
    IF `notice of the meeting and of the resolution is given in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles`
        AND `the meeting is held and conducted in accordance with this Chapter (and, where relevant, Chapter 4) and the company's articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution of the members of a company is validly passed at a general meeting if—" -- MARGINAL a

§§ `Calling meetings`

-- ---- s 302 Directors' power to call general meetings -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3896 | The directors of a company may call a general meeting of the company.
@ref s 302 Directors' power to call general meetings (src:3896)
GIVEN `the person calling the meeting is a director of the company acting as one of its directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 302 the directors may call a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the person calling the meeting is a director of the company acting as one of its directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors of a company may call a general meeting of the company"

-- ---- s 303 Members' power to require directors to call general meeting -------------------------------------

-- src:3898 | (1) The members of a company may require the directors to call a general meeting of the company.
@ref s 303(1) Members' power to require directors to call general meeting (src:3898)
GIVEN `the persons requiring the meeting are members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(1) the members may require the directors to call a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the persons requiring the meeting are members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a company may require the directors to call a general meeting of the company"

-- Fractions: 0.05 is 5%. For a company with a share capital the measure is paid-up capital carrying the right of voting
-- at general meetings (treasury shares excluded); otherwise it is the total voting rights of the members with a right to vote.
-- src:3899 | (2) The directors are required to call a general meeting once the company has received requests to do so from—
-- src:3900 | (a) members representing at least 5% of such of the paid-up capital of the company as carries the right of voting at general meetings of the company (excluding any paid-up capital held as treasury shares); or
-- src:3901 | (b) in the case of a company not having a share capital, members who represent at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at general meetings.
@ref s 303(2) Members' power to require directors to call general meeting: the requests (src:3899-3901)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid-up capital held by the requesting members that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `paid-up capital of the company that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `voting rights represented by the requesting members` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at general meetings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(2) the directors are required to call a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital`
    THEN IF `paid-up capital held by the requesting members that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `paid-up capital of the company that carries the right of voting at general meetings (excluding treasury shares)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors are required to call a general meeting once the company has received requests to do so from— (a) members representing at least 5% of such of the paid-up capital of the company as carries the right of voting at general meetings" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `voting rights represented by the requesting members` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at general meetings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a company not having a share capital, members who represent at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at general meetings" -- MARGINAL a

-- (3) is shown blank in the text: "(3) . . . . . ." (repealed or omitted; nothing to encode)

-- src:3904 | (a) must state the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting, and
@ref s 303(4)(a) Members' power to require directors to call general meeting: the business (src:3904)
GIVEN `the request states the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(4)(a) the request meets this requirement` MEANS
    IF `the request states the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A request— (a) must state the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- (5) a resolution may properly be moved at a meeting unless it is ineffective, defamatory, or frivolous or vexatious.
-- src:3906 | (5) A resolution may properly be moved at a meeting unless—
-- src:3907 | (a) it would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise),
-- src:3908 | (b) it is defamatory of any person, or
-- src:3909 | (c) it is frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 303(5) Members' power to require directors to call general meeting: a resolution that may properly be moved (src:3906-3909)
GIVEN `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is defamatory of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(5) the resolution may properly be moved at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the resolution would, if passed, be ineffective (whether by reason of inconsistency with any enactment or the company's constitution or otherwise)`
        OR `the resolution is defamatory of any person`
        OR `the resolution is frivolous or vexatious`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution may properly be moved at a meeting unless— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3905 | (b) may include the text of a resolution that may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at the meeting.
@ref s 303(4)(b) Members' power to require directors to call general meeting: the text of a resolution (src:3905)
GIVEN `the resolution may properly be moved at the meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is intended to be moved at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(4)(b) the request may include the text of the resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution is intended to be moved at the meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may include the text of a resolution that may properly be moved and is intended to be moved at the meeting"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the resolution may properly be moved at the meeting`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a resolution that may properly be moved" -- MARGINAL b

-- src:3910 | (6) A request—
-- src:3911 | (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form, and
-- src:3912 | (b) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it.
@ref s 303(6) Members' power to require directors to call general meeting: the form of the request (src:3910-3912)
GIVEN `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(6) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A request— (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form"
    ELSE IF `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 304 Directors' duty to call meetings required by members --------------------------------------------

-- "within 21 days from the date on which they become subject to the requirement": the last day is that date plus 21 (fork F7).
-- src:3914 | (1) Directors required under section 303 to call a general meeting of the company must call a meeting—
-- src:3915 | (a) within 21 days from the date on which they become subject to the requirement, and
@ref s 304(1)(a) Directors' duty to call meetings required by members: within 21 days (src:3914-3915)
GIVEN `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement under section 303` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the directors called the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(1)(a) the directors called the meeting in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the directors called the meeting` AT MOST `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement under section 303` PLUS 21
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must call a meeting— (a) within 21 days from the date on which they become subject to the requirement" -- FORK F7

-- src:3916 | (b) to be held on a date not more than 28 days after the date of the notice convening the meeting.
@ref s 304(1)(b) Directors' duty to call meetings required by members: held within 28 days of the notice (src:3916)
GIVEN `the date of the notice convening the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the meeting is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(1)(b) the meeting is to be held in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the meeting is to be held` AT MOST `the date of the notice convening the meeting` PLUS 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) to be held on a date not more than 28 days after the date of the notice convening the meeting" -- FORK F7

-- src:3917 | (2) If the requests received by the company identify a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting, the notice of the meeting must include notice of the resolution.
@ref s 304(2) Directors' duty to call meetings required by members: notice of the resolution (src:3917)
GIVEN `the requests received by the company identify a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(2) the notice of the meeting must include notice of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the requests received by the company identify a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the requests received by the company identify a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3918 | (3) The business that may be dealt with at the meeting includes a resolution of which notice is given in accordance with this section.
@ref s 304(3) Directors' duty to call meetings required by members: the business (src:3918)
GIVEN `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(3) the resolution is business that may be dealt with at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The business that may be dealt with at the meeting includes a resolution of which notice is given in accordance with this section"

-- src:3919 | (4) If the resolution is to be proposed as a special resolution, the directors are treated as not having duly called the meeting if they do not give the required notice of the resolution in accordance with section 283.
@ref s 304(4) Directors' duty to call meetings required by members: a special resolution (src:3919)
GIVEN `the resolution is to be proposed as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors give the required notice of the resolution in accordance with section 283` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(4) the directors are treated as not having duly called the meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the resolution is to be proposed as a special resolution`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the resolution is to be proposed as a special resolution" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the directors give the required notice of the resolution in accordance with section 283`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors are treated as not having duly called the meeting if they do not give the required notice" -- MARGINAL a
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 305 Power of members to call meeting at company's expense -------------------------------------------

-- The members who requested the meeting may call it themselves, or any of them representing more than one half of the
-- total voting rights of all of them.
-- src:3921 | (1) If the directors—
-- src:3922 | (a) are required under section 303 to call a meeting, and
-- src:3923 | (b) do not do so in accordance with section 304,
-- src:3924 | the members who requested the meeting, or any of them representing more than one half of the total voting rights of all of them, may themselves call a general meeting.
@ref s 305(1) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense (src:3921-3924)
GIVEN `the directors are required under section 303 to call a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors do not call the meeting in accordance with section 304` IS A BOOLEAN
      `voting rights represented by the members who call the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members who requested the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(1) the members may themselves call a general meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the directors are required under section 303 to call a meeting`) OR (NOT `the directors do not call the meeting in accordance with section 304`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the directors— (a) are required under section 303 to call a meeting, and (b) do not do so in accordance with section 304" -- FORK F22 -- MARGINAL b
    ELSE IF `voting rights represented by the members who call the meeting` AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members who requested the meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `voting rights represented by the members who call the meeting` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `total voting rights of all the members who requested the meeting`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the members who requested the meeting, or any of them representing more than one half of the total voting rights of all of them"

-- src:3925 | (2) Where the requests received by the company included the text of a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting, the notice of the meeting must include notice of the resolution.
@ref s 305(2) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense: notice of the resolution (src:3925)
GIVEN `the requests received by the company included the text of a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(2) the notice of the meeting must include notice of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the requests received by the company included the text of a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the requests received by the company included the text of a resolution intended to be moved at the meeting" -- MARGINAL a

-- "not more than three months after": the latest date is the date the directors became subject to the requirement plus three months.
-- src:3926 | (3) The meeting must be called for a date not more than three months after the date on which the directors become subject to the requirement to call a meeting.
@ref s 305(3) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense: three months (src:3926)
GIVEN `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement to call a meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the meeting is called` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(3) the meeting is called for a date in time` MEANS
    IF `the date for which the meeting is called` AT MOST `add months` `the date on which the directors became subject to the requirement to call a meeting` 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The meeting must be called for a date not more than three months after the date on which the directors become subject to the requirement to call a meeting" -- FORK F7

-- src:3927 | (4) The meeting must be called in the same manner, as nearly as possible, as that in which meetings are required to be called by directors of the company.
@ref s 305(4) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense: the manner (src:3927)
GIVEN `the meeting is called in the same manner, as nearly as possible, as that in which meetings are required to be called by directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(4) the meeting is called in the manner this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is called in the same manner, as nearly as possible, as that in which meetings are required to be called by directors of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The meeting must be called in the same manner, as nearly as possible, as that in which meetings are required to be called by directors of the company" -- FORK F5

-- src:3928 | (5) The business which may be dealt with at the meeting includes a resolution of which notice is given in accordance with this section.
@ref s 305(5) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense: the business (src:3928)
GIVEN `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(5) the resolution is business that may be dealt with at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `notice of the resolution is given in accordance with this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The business which may be dealt with at the meeting includes a resolution of which notice is given in accordance with this section"

-- src:3929 | (6) Any reasonable expenses incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting must be reimbursed by the company.
@ref s 305(6) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense: reimbursement (src:3929)
GIVEN `the expenses were incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(6) the company must reimburse the expenses` MEANS
    IF `the expenses were incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting` AND `the expenses are reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any reasonable expenses incurred by the members requesting the meeting by reason of the failure of the directors duly to call a meeting must be reimbursed by the company"

-- src:3930 | (7) Any sum so reimbursed shall be retained by the company out of any sums due or to become due from the company by way of fees or other remuneration in respect of the services of such of the directors as were in default.
@ref s 305(7) Power of members to call meeting at company's expense: retention out of the directors' pay (src:3930)
GIVEN `the sum was reimbursed under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director was one of the directors in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305(7) the company shall retain the sum out of the sums due to the director` MEANS
    IF `the sum was reimbursed under subsection (6)` AND `the director was one of the directors in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "retained by the company out of any sums due or to become due from the company by way of fees or other remuneration in respect of the services of such of the directors as were in default"

-- ---- s 306 Power of court to order meeting -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3932 | (1) This section applies if for any reason it is impracticable—
-- src:3933 | (a) to call a meeting of a company in any manner in which meetings of that company may be called, or
-- src:3934 | (b) to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the company's articles or this Act.
@ref s 306(1) Power of court to order meeting: application (src:3932-3934)
GIVEN `it is impracticable to call a meeting of the company in any manner in which meetings of that company may be called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the company's articles or this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 306(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `it is impracticable to call a meeting of the company in any manner in which meetings of that company may be called`
        OR `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the company's articles or this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if for any reason it is impracticable— (a) ... or (b) ..." -- MARGINAL a

DECLARE `s 306(2) who moves the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 306(2) the court of its own motion`
    `s 306(2)(a) a director of the company`
    `s 306(2)(b) a member of the company who would be entitled to vote at the meeting`
    `s 306(2) another person`

-- src:3935 | (2) The court may, either of its own motion or on the application—
-- src:3936 | (a) of a director of the company, or
-- src:3937 | (b) of a member of the company who would be entitled to vote at the meeting,
-- src:3938 | order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in any manner the court thinks fit.
@ref s 306(2) Power of court to order meeting: the order (src:3935-3938)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      mover IS A `s 306(2) who moves the court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 306(2) the court may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in any manner the court thinks fit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies if for any reason it is impracticable" -- FORK F22 -- MARGINAL b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER mover
        WHEN `s 306(2) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "either of its own motion or on the application— (a) of a director of the company, or (b) of a member of the company who would be entitled to vote at the meeting"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3939 | (3) Where such an order is made, the court may give such ancillary or consequential directions as it thinks expedient.
@ref s 306(3) Power of court to order meeting: ancillary directions (src:3939)
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 306(3) the court may give ancillary or consequential directions` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where such an order is made" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:3940 | (4) Such directions may include a direction that one member of the company present at the meeting be deemed to constitute a quorum.
@ref s 306(4) Power of court to order meeting: a quorum of one (src:3940)
GIVEN `the directions are given under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 306(4) the directions may include a direction that one member present be deemed to constitute a quorum` MEANS
    IF `the directions are given under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such directions may include a direction that one member of the company present at the meeting be deemed to constitute a quorum"

-- src:3941 | (5) A meeting called, held and conducted in accordance with an order under this section is deemed for all purposes to be a meeting of the company duly called, held and conducted.
@ref s 306(5) Power of court to order meeting: effect of the order (src:3941)
GIVEN `the meeting is called, held and conducted in accordance with an order under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 306(5) the meeting is deemed for all purposes to be a meeting of the company duly called, held and conducted` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is called, held and conducted in accordance with an order under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A meeting called, held and conducted in accordance with an order under this section is deemed for all purposes to be a meeting of the company duly called, held and conducted"
